@@@!atrep

@@/ at-aphanes: the unseen pack (ἀφανής, not appearing) -
@@/ editorial metadata that never reaches the page: who speaks a
@@/ line of prose dialogue, whom or what a name denotes, the
@@/ canonical target of a reference, the normalized value of a
@@/ date, the analytic category of a span. TEI's attributes in
@@/ atrep's grammar: the key is the sim, the value the
@@/ parameter, one monosim per fact - never key=value inside a
@@/ parameter.
@@/ Every sim is a monosim, so litosis strips the whole pack: a
@@/ kanon composed with at-aphanes has the same litos as the
@@/ bare kanon. Anything that would need grammata is by
@@/ definition not aphanes material. Where content is printed
@@/ (an apparatus, a note, a speech prefix) the host dialektos
@@/ owns it; aphanes carries only what the eye never sees.
@@/ Placement: an aphanes monosim annotates the simmere whose
@@/ inline content directly holds it - written first inside the
@@/ grammata of an endo-simmere or paragraph, or in a
@@/ para-simmere's lemma. Exomorphoses read it from there
@@/ through the sim-name slot: @(prosopon) in a rule template
@@/ fills who="..." on the element the rule emits, and the
@@/ monosim's own rule renders nothing.
@@/ Values are free keys in this edition (the index-hidden
@@/ model); a document that declares dramatis personae may
@@/ validate prosopon keys against them (host-side constraint).
@@/ Keys live in the onym namespace: kanonizo rewrites a key that
@@/ names a declared numbered onym, and leaves autonyms and free
@@/ keys alone.
@@/ Part of the standard library; composes with koine and its
@@/ sibling packs. The pair of the diaphane: a diaphane shows
@@/ its content through, aphanes shows nothing at all.

@=== prosopon
@?:(who)
@"the person: who speaks this line, or whom this name denotes"@
@""
πρόσωπον, the person, the dramatic character (τὰ τοῦ δράματος
πρόσωπα is the dramatis personae). Inside a prose dialogue line
it names the speaker; inside a name span, the referent. TEI
said/@who, q/@who, sp/@who, persName/@ref. In drama the speech
prefix (the dialogue lemma) carries the speaker, and a speech
without a prosopon is attributed by its prefix alone. Where the
source points at a character the prosopon is written first in
the lemma (@: @?:(barnardo)BARNARDO.) and gives the key the
printed prefix cannot: prefixes are abbreviated, punctuated and
respelled, keys are not.
""@
===@

@=== chora
@?.(where)
@"the place a name denotes"@
@""
χώρα, place, land, country. TEI placeName/@ref.
""@
===@

@=== syllogos
@?&(which)
@"the body (organisation, group, institution) a name denotes"@
@""
σύλλογος, an assembly, association, society. TEI orgName/@ref.
""@
===@

@=== skopos
@?>(target)
@"the canonical target of a reference: a coordinate, an address"@
@""
σκοπός, the mark aimed at. The pointer's target in a citation
scheme rather than an onym of this document: a scripture
reference in OSIS spelling (Gen.1.1-Gen.1.3), a URI, a
canonical section address. TEI ref/@target, USX ref/@loc,
OSIS reference/@osisRef. One per span; the wording of the
reference stays printed text.
""@
===@

@=== chronos
@?-(when)
@"the normalized value of a date or time (ISO 8601)"@
@""
χρόνος, time. TEI date/@when. An ISO 8601 date, datetime, or
interval (1813-01-28/1813-02-01) - no whitespace. The date's
wording stays printed text.
""@
===@

@=== eidos
@?%(category)
@"an analytic category the annotated span belongs to"@
@""
εἶδος, kind, class. TEI @ana: stylometric and discourse
categories, standoff interpretation. Repeatable: one monosim
per category; the sim-name slot joins them with spaces.
""@
===@

@=== paradosis
@?~(reading)
@"the transmitted reading: what the page prints where the text gives the editor's form"@
@""
παράδοσις, what is handed down, the transmitted text as
against the emendation. TEI choice: the text carries expan,
corr or reg, and the abbr, sic or orig it stands for is the
paradosis of the diaphane around it (@@.@?~(ye\ olde)the
old.@@). A space in the value is written escaped, with the
inactive sigil before it, and is a literal space to every
reader. The TEI exo writes the pair back as a choice, the
paradosis as orig and the reading as reg; which of abbr, sic
or orig the source used is not kept.
""@
===@
